Feature: Calculate Total Time Elapsed (TAT) for New Enrollment Review in tat_report

  Background:
    Given Unity Catalog "purgo_databricks" and Schema "purgo_playground" are available
    And pat_case table exists in purgo_playground schema
    And sr_activity table exists in purgo_playground schema
    And tat_report table will be created in purgo_playground schema, overwriting any existing table

  # Happy Path: Valid Start and End Dates, End Date >= Start Date, No NULLs, Weekends excluded
  Scenario Outline: Calculate total_time_elapsed for valid New Enrollment Review cases
    Given a pat_case record with
      | case_id         | <case_id>         |
      | service_request_type | "Patient Foundation" |
      | sr_created_date | <sr_created_date> |
    And one or more sr_activity records exist for case_id <case_id> with
      | subject         | "Perform New Enrollment Review Activity" |
      | status          | "Completed"                              |
      | last_modified_date | <last_modified_date_1>                |
      | last_modified_date | <last_modified_date_2>                |
    When the minimum last_modified_date for the case_id is <expected_end_date>
    And both sr_created_date and minimum last_modified_date are not NULL
    And minimum last_modified_date >= sr_created_date
    Then total_time_elapsed is calculated as the number of working days (excluding Saturdays and Sundays) between sr_created_date (date only) and minimum last_modified_date (date only)
    And total_time_elapsed is an integer
    And tat_report contains all columns from pat_case plus total_time_elapsed

    Examples:
      | case_id | sr_created_date | last_modified_date_1 | last_modified_date_2 | expected_end_date | expected_total_time_elapsed |
      | 1001    | 2024-06-01      | 2024-06-05          | 2024-06-03           | 2024-06-03        | 1                          |
      | 1002    | 2024-06-07      | 2024-06-10          | 2024-06-12           | 2024-06-10        | 1                          |
      | 1003    | 2024-06-14      | 2024-06-17          | 2024-06-18           | 2024-06-17        | 1                          |

  # Edge Case: End Date < Start Date
  Scenario Outline: End Date is before Start Date
    Given a pat_case record with
      | case_id         | <case_id>         |
      | service_request_type | "Patient Foundation" |
      | sr_created_date | <sr_created_date> |
    And one sr_activity record exists for case_id <case_id> with
      | subject         | "Perform New Enrollment Review Activity" |
      | status          | "Completed"                              |
      | last_modified_date | <last_modified_date>                  |
    When minimum last_modified_date < sr_created_date
    Then total_time_elapsed is NULL
    And tat_report contains all columns from pat_case plus total_time_elapsed

    Examples:
      | case_id | sr_created_date | last_modified_date | expected_total_time_elapsed |
      | 2001    | 2024-06-10      | 2024-06-08        | NULL                       |

  # Edge Case: End Date = Start Date
  Scenario Outline: End Date equals Start Date
    Given a pat_case record with
      | case_id         | <case_id>         |
      | service_request_type | "Patient Foundation" |
      | sr_created_date | <sr_created_date> |
    And one sr_activity record exists for case_id <case_id> with
      | subject         | "Perform New Enrollment Review Activity" |
      | status          | "Completed"                              |
      | last_modified_date | <last_modified_date>                  |
    When minimum last_modified_date = sr_created_date
    Then total_time_elapsed is 0
    And tat_report contains all columns from pat_case plus total_time_elapsed

    Examples:
      | case_id | sr_created_date | last_modified_date | expected_total_time_elapsed |
      | 3001    | 2024-06-10      | 2024-06-10        | 0                          |

  # Error Case: Start Date or End Date is NULL
  Scenario Outline: Start Date or End Date is NULL
    Given a pat_case record with
      | case_id         | <case_id>         |
      | service_request_type | "Patient Foundation" |
      | sr_created_date | <sr_created_date> |
    And one sr_activity record exists for case_id <case_id> with
      | subject         | "Perform New Enrollment Review Activity" |
      | status          | "Completed"                              |
      | last_modified_date | <last_modified_date>                  |
    When sr_created_date is NULL or minimum last_modified_date is NULL
    Then total_time_elapsed is NULL
    And tat_report contains all columns from pat_case plus total_time_elapsed

    Examples:
      | case_id | sr_created_date | last_modified_date | expected_total_time_elapsed |
      | 4001    | NULL            | 2024-06-10        | NULL                       |
      | 4002    | 2024-06-10      | NULL              | NULL                       |

  # Error Case: No matching sr_activity record for case_id
  Scenario Outline: No matching sr_activity record for case_id
    Given a pat_case record with
      | case_id         | <case_id>         |
      | service_request_type | "Patient Foundation" |
      | sr_created_date | <sr_created_date> |
    And no sr_activity record exists for case_id <case_id> with
      | subject         | "Perform New Enrollment Review Activity" |
      | status          | "Completed"                              |
    Then total_time_elapsed is NULL
    And tat_report contains all columns from pat_case plus total_time_elapsed

    Examples:
      | case_id | sr_created_date | expected_total_time_elapsed |
      | 5001    | 2024-06-10      | NULL                       |

  # Error Case: pat_case.service_request_type is not "Patient Foundation"
  Scenario Outline: pat_case record with non-matching service_request_type
    Given a pat_case record with
      | case_id         | <case_id>         |
      | service_request_type | <service_request_type> |
      | sr_created_date | <sr_created_date> |
    And one sr_activity record exists for case_id <case_id> with
      | subject         | "Perform New Enrollment Review Activity" |
      | status          | "Completed"                              |
      | last_modified_date | <last_modified_date>                  |
    When service_request_type is not "Patient Foundation"
    Then tat_report does not include this pat_case record

    Examples:
      | case_id | service_request_type | sr_created_date | last_modified_date |
      | 6001    | "Other Type"         | 2024-06-10      | 2024-06-12        |

  # Error Case: sr_activity.subject or status does not match
  Scenario Outline: sr_activity record with non-matching subject or status
    Given a pat_case record with
      | case_id         | <case_id>         |
      | service_request_type | "Patient Foundation" |
      | sr_created_date | <sr_created_date> |
    And one sr_activity record exists for case_id <case_id> with
      | subject         | <subject>         |
      | status          | <status>          |
      | last_modified_date | <last_modified_date>                  |
    When subject is not "Perform New Enrollment Review Activity" or status is not "Completed"
    Then tat_report does not include this pat_case record

    Examples:
      | case_id | subject                          | status      | sr_created_date | last_modified_date |
      | 7001    | "Other Activity"                 | "Completed" | 2024-06-10      | 2024-06-12        |
      | 7002    | "Perform New Enrollment Review Activity" | "In Progress" | 2024-06-10      | 2024-06-12        |

  # Validation: total_time_elapsed is always integer or NULL
  Scenario Outline: Validate total_time_elapsed data type
    Given tat_report contains a record for case_id <case_id>
    Then total_time_elapsed is either an integer or NULL

    Examples:
      | case_id | expected_total_time_elapsed |
      | 8001    | 2                          |
      | 8002    | NULL                       |

  # Validation: Only working days are counted (weekends excluded)
  Scenario Outline: Weekend adjustment in total_time_elapsed calculation
    Given sr_created_date is <start_date> and minimum last_modified_date is <end_date>
    When calculating total_time_elapsed
    Then only weekdays (Monday to Friday) between start_date and end_date (inclusive) are counted
    And Saturdays and Sundays are excluded

    Examples:
      | start_date | end_date   | expected_total_time_elapsed |
      | 2024-06-07 | 2024-06-10 | 1                          | # 2024-06-08 (Sat), 2024-06-09 (Sun) excluded
      | 2024-06-14 | 2024-06-17 | 1                          | # 2024-06-15 (Sat), 2024-06-16 (Sun) excluded

  # Validation: tat_report includes all columns from pat_case plus total_time_elapsed
  Scenario: tat_report schema validation
    Given tat_report is created
    Then tat_report contains all columns from pat_case
    And tat_report contains total_time_elapsed column

  # Validation: tat_report is overwritten on each run
  Scenario: tat_report overwrite behavior
    Given tat_report exists in purgo_playground schema
    When the PySpark script is executed
    Then tat_report is overwritten with new results

